      "worked_solution": "Any point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = \\sin\\theta\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225445/assets/f438a90ea7afe511562058f49f13af29722aa137a8032a22ac16ca6566688cb7.png)\n\nWe're given that $x=-0.7$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = -0.7.\n$$",
